<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Evaluation Prompts</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section provides the prompts used for both evaluation tasks, addressing reviewer requests for complete methodological transparency. Table <a href="#A4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Appendix D Evaluation Prompts ‣ Know Thyself? On the Incapability and Implications of AI Self-Recognition" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> shows the prompts we used for the binary self-recognition task. Table <a href="#A4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Appendix D Evaluation Prompts ‣ Know Thyself? On the Incapability and Implications of AI Self-Recognition" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> shows the prompts used for the model prediction task. In Table <a href="#A4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix D Evaluation Prompts ‣ Know Thyself? On the Incapability and Implications of AI Self-Recognition" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we also provide the prompts that we used to evaluate model’s awareness of existence and reasoning patterns.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>Prompts used for the binary self-recognition task. [TEXT] is replaced with the actual generated text sample.</figcaption>
